ware companies race headcount and burn, Basecamp has run the same playbook for two decades: a handful of products, profitable every year, no growth theater. Why the calm model is newly relevant for founders in 2026.\",\"datePublished\":\"2026-09-29\",\"dateModified\":\"2026-09-27T23:52:05.850Z\",\"inLanguage\":[\"en\",\"fa\"],\"articleSection\":\"Startups\",\"keywords\":\"startups, bootstrapping\",\"author\":{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"Mehrdad\",\"url\":\"https://mehrdad.ir/about\"},\"publisher\":{\"@type\":\"Person\",\"name\":\"Mehrdad\",\"url\":\"https://mehrdad.ir\"},\"mainEntityOfPage\":\"https://mehrdad.ir/daily/calm-company-basecamp\"}</script><script type=\"application/ld+json\">{\"@context\":\"https://schema.org\",\"@type\":\"BreadcrumbList\",\"itemListElement\":[{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":1,\"name\":\"Home\",\"item\":\"https://mehrdad.ir/\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":2,\"name\":\"Daily\",\"item\":\"https://mehrdad.ir/daily\"},{\"@type\":\"ListItem\",\"position\":3,\"name\":\"Basecamp keeps proving calm companies outlast blitzscaled ones\",\"item\":\"https://mehrdad.ir/daily/calm-company-basecamp\"}]}</script><article class=\"mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pb-16 sm:px-6\"><nav aria-label=\"Breadcrumb\" class=\"flex items-center gap-1 pt-8 text-sm text-muted-foreground\"><a class=\"transition-colors hover:text-foreground\" href=\"/daily\">All analyses</a><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-chevron-right h-3.5 w-3.5 rtl:rotate-180\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"></path></svg><span class=\"truncate text-foreground/80\">Basecamp keeps proving calm companies outlast blitzscaled ones</span></nav><header class=\"mt-6\"><div class=\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-1 text-xs text-muted-foreground\"><time dateTime=\"2026-09-29\">Sep 29, 2026</time><a class=\"font-medium text-violet-600 transition-colors hover:text-violet-500 dark:text-violet-400\" href=\"/daily/cat/startup\">Startups</a><span>#<!-- -->startups</span><span>#<!-- -->bootstrapping</span></div><h1 class=\"mt-3 text-3xl font-extrabold leading-tight sm:text-4xl\">Basecamp keeps proving calm companies outlast blitzscaled ones</h1></header><aside aria-label=\"In short\" class=\"mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-border bg-muted/40 p-4 sm:p-5\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-muted-foreground\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-list-ordered h-4 w-4\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M10 12h11\"></path><path d=\"M10 18h11\"></path><path d=\"M10 6h11\"></path><path d=\"M4 10h2\"></path><path d=\"M4 6h1v4\"></path><path d=\"M6 18H4c0-1 2-2 2-3s-1-1.5-2-1\"></path></svg>In short</div><p class=\"mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-foreground/90\" dir=\"ltr\">While most software companies race headcount and burn, Basecamp has run the same playbook for two decades: a handful of products, profitable every year, no growth theater. Why the calm model is newly relevant for founders in 2026.</p></aside><div class=\"prose-blog mt-8\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>The dominant startup story of the last fifteen years says grow or die: raise big and hire fast and figure out revenue later. Basecamp never subscribed. The company stayed small on purpose and profitable on purpose and kept its product surface almost unchanged while entire categories around it boomed and collapsed.</p>\n<h2>What the calm company actually optimizes</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Profit over headcount.</strong> Every new hire must remove more work than they add.</li>\n<li><strong>Few products kept excellent.</strong> The lineup stays short — the maintenance burden stays survivable.</li>\n<li><strong>No growth theater.</strong> Metrics that do not touch the bank account are not celebrated.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2>Why this reads differently in 2026</h2>\n<p>Every year the cost story of running software shifts. Talent is expensive and customer acquisition is expensive and investors have stopped rewarding pure growth. In that climate the calm playbook stops looking conservative and starts looking like arbitrage: a two-person team with a profitable product can survive decades that kill venture-funded competitors. I see the same pattern in miniature among the <a href=\"/work\" rel=\"noopener\">small products I build</a> — a narrow profitable tool outlives three flashy experiments.</p>\n<h2>The honest limitations</h2>\n<p>Calm is not free. Markets that demand rapid scale pass such companies by and some categories genuinely need blitzscale to exist at all. A calm company also caps its own upside — nobody buys a private island on Basecamp margins. The model is a values decision as much as a strategy one.</p></div><section aria-label=\"My expert take\" class=\"mt-10 rounded-2xl border border-violet-500/40 bg-violet-500/5 p-4 sm:p-6\"><div class=\"flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-bold text-violet-700 dark:text-violet-300\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-graduation-cap h-5 w-5\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"M21.42 10.922a1 1 0 0 0-.019-1.838L12.83 5.18a2 2 0 0 0-1.66 0L2.6 9.08a1 1 0 0 0 0 1.832l8.57 3.908a2 2 0 0 0 1.66 0z\"></path><path d=\"M22 10v6\"></path><path d=\"M6 12.5V16a6 3 0 0 0 12 0v-3.5\"></path></svg>My expert take</div><div class=\"prose-blog mt-2\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>Two decades of profitability without a growth machine is the strongest possible evidence for the calm model and almost nobody copies it — because it is boring and boring does not trend. My take for founders building in 2026: decide early whether you are building a rocket or a house. Rockets need fuel and a launch window. Houses need a foundation and a roof that does not leak. Both are valid. Pretending your house is a rocket is what kills companies.</p></div></section><div class=\"mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-2\"><span data-slot=\"badge\" class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-md border px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium w-fit whitespace-nowrap shrink-0 [&amp;&gt;svg]:size-3 gap-1 [&amp;&gt;svg]:pointer-events-none focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-[3px] aria-invalid:ring-destructive/20 dark:aria-invalid:ring-destructive/40 aria-invalid:border-destructive transition-[color,box-shadow] overflow-hidden [a&amp;]:hover:bg-accent [a&amp;]:hover:text-accent-foreground border-fuchsia-500/30 text-fuchsia-700 dark:text-fuchsia-300\">#<!-- -->startups</span><span data-slot=\"badge\" class=\"inline-flex items-center justify-center rounded-md border px-2 py-0.5 text-xs font-medium w-fit whitespace-nowrap shrink-0 [&amp;&gt;svg]:size-3 gap-1 [&amp;&gt;svg]:pointer-events-none focus-visible:border-ring focus-visible:ring-ring/50 focus-visible:ring-[3px] aria-invalid:ring-destructive/20 dark:aria-invalid:ring-destructive/40 aria-invalid:border-destructive transition-[color,box-shadow] overflow-hidden [a&amp;]:hover:bg-accent [a&amp;]:hover:text-accent-foreground border-fuchsia-500/30 text-fuchsia-700 dark:text-fuchsia-300\">#<!-- -->bootstrapping</span></div><div class=\"mt-8 border-y border-border py-4\"><div class=\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2\" aria-label=\"Share this article\"><span class=\"text-xs font-semibold text-muted-foreground\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" class=\"lucide lucide-share2 lucide-share-2 me-1.5 inline h-3.5 w-3.5\" aria-hidd